.TH CVVERSIONS 1 "April 2017" "Xsan File System"
.SH NAME
cvversions \- Display Xsan client/server versions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.na
.nh
.HP
.B cvversions [ -h ] [ -F \fItype\fP ] [[\fIid\fP:]\fIfile ...\fP]
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcvversions\fR will display the revision, build level and creation
date for the \fIFile System Manager (FSM)\fR and client subsystems of
the \fIXsan File System\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "-h"
Print a help/usage message and exit.
.IP "-F \fItype\fP"
If \fItype\fP is \fBtext\fP, cvversions emits version information in text format
(this is the default).
If \fItype\fP is \fBjson\fP, cvversions emits limited version information in a parsable JSON format.
.IP file
.I file
is searched for a Xsan version string and, if found,
is printed in addition to the standard version strings.
If present in the argument, \fIid\fP is substituted for \fIfile\fP in the
program output.
.SH USAGE
Simply execute the program and record the information shown.
